# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out however
# the platform wants them. Without this, the first commit from a machine with a
# different autocrlf setting rewrites every file in the repo and buries the real
# change in it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated, and noisy in a diff.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff

# The delivered design. Git would detect these as binary anyway, but the .fig is
# the only copy of what the designer drew — it does not get to depend on that.
*.png binary
*.fig binary

# Windows scripts stay CRLF in every checkout. The rest of the repo is LF, but
# wscript and cmd are the two tools that still care, and a supervisor that fails
# to parse fails silently: the scheduled task reports success and nothing runs.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
